    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6033" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caelĭmontĭum</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coel-</span></b> ), ii,
			n.
		Caelius-mons, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the second region of Rome</i>, <i>including the Cœlian Hill</i>, P. Vict. Reg. Urb.
			R.—Hence, adj.: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caelĭmontānus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Coel-</span></b> ), a, um, <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to
				Cœlimontium</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">porta,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Pis. 23, 55</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">CAMPVS,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell. 2617</span></i>
			.</div>
